CGTK 1.4
========

CGTK, the Classic GUI Toolkit, is a fork of GTK+ 1.2.10 and GLib 1.2.10,
the last releases of the GTK+ 1.2 series, kept building and working on
current systems. The libraries, headers, functions and types keep
their GTK+ and GLib names, so that programs written for GTK+ 1.2 build
against it with few changes or none.

It is not GTK+, and it is not maintained by the GTK+ or GNOME projects.
Please do not report its bugs to them.

Installation
============

See the file INSTALL.

Changes
=======

What has changed since GTK+ 1.2.10 and GLib 1.2.10 is in ChangeLog.

Example programs to build against CGTK are in examples/; see
examples/README.

History
=======

GTK+ and GLib were written by Peter Mattis, Spencer Kimball, Josh
MacDonald and the GTK+ team, and many others who sent patches. Their
README, NEWS, ChangeLog, AUTHORS and other notes, as released with
GTK+ 1.2.10 and GLib 1.2.10, are in history/gtk+ and history/glib,
unchanged.

Licence
=======

The libraries are under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version
2.1 or (at your option) any later version; see COPYING. The files that
came from GTK+ and GLib say version 2 or any later version of the
Library GPL, of which the Lesser GPL 2.1 is the next version, and the
files written or ported since say 2.1 or later, so 2.1 or later covers
them all together.

cgtk-theme, the theme editor, is under the same licence. An example that
names a licence of its own is under that one.

GDK's SVG renderer, gdk/nanosvg.h and gdk/nanosvgrast.h, came from
NanoSVG, by Mikko Mononen, and is under the zlib licence given at the
top of each.
